---
alwaysApply: true
---

When writing code:

1. Check for existing files and logic first thoroughly every time
2. DO NOT create new files without checking for existing files and logic
3. ONLY create new files if 100% sure no existing logic exists OR when existing files are >250 lines of code
4. If existing file size is >250 lines of code, create a new file and import where necessary

Priority #1 is not to create duplicate, conflicting code or copy code that exists into 2 different files where it might compete or repeat.